```ADD_PAPER
2502.00640v3
The paper "CollabLLM: From Passive Responders to Active Collaborators" proposes a novel training framework that transforms large language models from passive responders to proactive collaborators through the use of a collaborative simulation framework that estimates long-term, multiturn-aware rewards. By reinforcing these rewards during fine-tuning, the framework enables the model to better uncover user intent and generate insightful suggestions, significantly improving multiturn interactions. Extensive experimental evaluations demonstrate an 18.5% increase in task performance and a 46.3% boost in interactivity, as judged by LLM evaluators. Additionally, a comprehensive user study with 201 participants confirmed that the model improves user satisfaction by 17.6% while reducing interaction time by 10.4%. These experimental results highlight the potential of multiturn-aware reward mechanisms to enhance collaborative tasks, such as document editing, code generation, and math problem solving, marking a promising advancement in human-LLM collaboration.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
