```ADD_PAPER
2405.19444v1
The paper "MathChat: Benchmarking Mathematical Reasoning and Instruction Following in Multi-Turn Interactions" introduces a comprehensive benchmark tailored to assess the capabilities of large language models in sustained, interactive mathematical problem solving. It highlights how current models, while effective at single-turn tasks, struggle with the nuances of multiturn dialogues that necessitate iterative clarifications and reasoning, a challenge shared with applications like document editing and code generation. By introducing the MathChat sync dataset—a synthetic dialogue resource designed for fine-tuning—this study demonstrates that prompt engineering based on interactive, multiturn data can significantly improve a model's ability to understand and follow complex instructions over several turns. Detailed experimental results show improved performance on intricate math tasks when models are exposed to these refined, conversational prompts, offering a strong foundation for developing multiturn-aware reward strategies in collaborative simulation settings.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
