```ADD_PAPER
2507.02256v1
The paper "Uncertainty-aware Reward Design Process" proposes a pioneering framework that fuses large language model reasoning with uncertainty estimation to autonomously design and fine-tune reward functions in reinforcement learning settings. By leveraging prompt engineering in a collaborative simulation context, the approach refines reward components over multiple turns, making it highly applicable to tasks like document editing, code generation, and interactive mathematical problem solving. The framework employs a bi-level optimization strategy that separates reward component tuning from hyperparameter configuration, resulting in marked improvements in reward quality and convergence speed. Experimentally, the method was validated across 35 diverse tasks, showing significant gains in both efficiency and accuracy, thus underscoring the potential of integrating multiturn-aware rewards to elevate human-LLM collaboration performance.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
