```ADD_PAPER
2408.12034v1
The paper "Enhancing LLM Collaboration through Targeted Prompt Engineering and Multiturn-aware Simulation" introduces a comprehensive framework that combines advanced reasoning techniques with iterative prompt engineering to maximize accuracy in multiturn human-LLM collaborations. Focusing on applications such as document editing, code generation, and math problem solving, the approach leverages a novel multiturn-aware rewards (MR) mechanism within a collaborative simulation environment. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method can improve task accuracy by up to 20% in document editing scenarios and reduce the number of corrective interactions by 15% in code generation tasks. Moreover, the framework shows strong performance consistency in complex mathematical problem solving by dynamically adapting reward signals based on evolving conversation contexts, leading to more precise and contextually appropriate responses. This work highlights the critical role of integrating targeted prompt engineering with reward-driven simulation for developing robust, task-aware LLM collaboration strategies.
``` 
